1
00:00:00,016 --> 00:00:01,016
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,016 --> 00:00:02,016
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,016 --> 00:00:03,583
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:07,383 --> 00:00:13,268
[Winter, 2011]

5
00:00:13,268 --> 00:00:17,840
Come on, I told you to order something
expensive. Get some boiled pork too.

6
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,424
You're a college student.
How much money could you have?

7
00:00:19,424 --> 00:00:21,412
It's fine. This is enough.

8
00:00:21,412 --> 00:00:23,684
I work part-time.

9
00:00:23,684 --> 00:00:25,252
I have more money than you.

10
00:00:25,252 --> 00:00:27,460
How? You're just
a civil service exam student.

11
00:00:27,460 --> 00:00:29,183
My mom.

12
00:00:29,936 --> 00:00:32,283
She's been saving up more than I realized.

13
00:00:35,448 --> 00:00:37,576
Is studying for the police exam going okay?

14
00:00:37,576 --> 00:00:38,940
I guess it's just right for me.

15
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:40,312
It really sticks in my head.

16
00:00:40,312 --> 00:00:41,736
Just wait and see.

17
00:00:41,736 --> 00:00:46,568
I'll be wearing a badge within two years,
and I'll catch that punk myself.

18
00:00:46,568 --> 00:00:48,560
And then what, after you catch him?

19
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,108
After that?

20
00:00:50,108 --> 00:00:51,376
Then I'll catch the next punk.

21
00:00:51,376 --> 00:00:53,116
Jeez, forget it, you punk.

22
00:00:53,748 --> 00:00:56,749
You talked me into being a reporter,
and now you're betraying me.

23
00:00:56,749 --> 00:00:58,149
The more I think about it,
the more pissed off I get.

24
00:00:58,149 --> 00:01:01,684
Hey, if we're all digging,
who's going to catch the fish?

25
00:01:01,684 --> 00:01:03,368
You just keep digging.

26
00:01:03,368 --> 00:01:05,124
I'll catch the fish.

27
00:01:05,124 --> 00:01:07,604
You do your job, and I'll do mine.

28
00:01:07,604 --> 00:01:09,136
Bang, bang!

29
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:10,244
Oh, please.

30
00:01:10,244 --> 00:01:12,704
Don't get beaten to a pulp
by some criminal later.

31
00:01:12,704 --> 00:01:15,688
- Ma'am, could you turn up the TV?
- Sure.

32
00:01:15,688 --> 00:01:18,169
[Police Focused on Kingfisher Investigation]
<i>The shooting incidents</i>

33
00:01:18,169 --> 00:01:22,100
<i>by the serial killer known as Kingfisher
have risen to nine.</i>

34
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:25,520
<i>Police have concluded that
last week's shooting in Cheongsin-dong</i>

35
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,556
[Kingfisher Shootings Rise to 9]
<i>was also the work of the same suspect.</i>

36
00:01:27,556 --> 00:01:30,383
[Cheongsin-dong Case Also Same Culprit]
<i>They are intensifying their investigation.</i>

37
00:01:30,383 --> 00:01:34,408
<i>Meanwhile, the number of members
in an online Kingfisher fan club</i>

38
00:01:34,408 --> 00:01:36,036
- <i>is approaching 300,000...</i>
- A fan club?

39
00:01:36,036 --> 00:01:37,683
Have they all lost their darn minds?

40
00:01:37,683 --> 00:01:39,583
Why are they cheering for that lunatic?

41
00:01:39,583 --> 00:01:42,020
Maybe they get
some kind of catharsis from it.

42
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:44,649
He picks out the worst criminals
and kills them.

43
00:01:44,649 --> 00:01:45,716
Catharsis, my foot.

44
00:01:45,716 --> 00:01:50,072
Hey, isn't killing a murderer still murder?

45
00:01:50,072 --> 00:01:52,320
Even if he only kills criminals for now,

46
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:54,783
who's to say he won't kill
an innocent person someday?

47
00:01:55,677 --> 00:01:59,649
If, by chance, I mean, seriously, what if...

48
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:04,248
just hypothetically,
Kingfisher killed that punk...

49
00:02:04,248 --> 00:02:06,183
That punk? Who...

50
00:02:08,549 --> 00:02:11,832
Do you really think
I'd feel happy or thankful?

51
00:02:11,832 --> 00:02:14,516
I mean, he'd be taking revenge
for you, or something like that.

52
00:02:14,516 --> 00:02:16,576
Darn it. Hey!

53
00:02:16,576 --> 00:02:20,244
If another murderer kills
my parents' murderer, is that revenge?

54
00:02:20,244 --> 00:02:22,048
If anyone's going to take revenge,
it should be me.

55
00:02:22,048 --> 00:02:24,216
What right does Kingfisher have?

56
00:02:30,096 --> 00:02:32,383
My revenge is

57
00:02:32,383 --> 00:02:36,116
to catch him and put him
in prison for the rest of his life.

58
00:02:36,116 --> 00:02:39,076
To me, they're both the same murdering punk.

59
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:41,608
Once I catch that punk,

60
00:02:41,608 --> 00:02:45,949
I'll catch Kingfisher next, no matter what.

61
00:02:46,852 --> 00:02:49,100
Just wait and see.

62
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,800
Alright.

63
00:02:55,149 --> 00:02:56,276
Oh, my.

64
00:02:56,276 --> 00:02:59,172
Oh, my, I'm so sorry.

65
00:02:59,172 --> 00:03:02,356
Ma'am, one plate of boiled pork, please.

66
00:03:02,356 --> 00:03:03,776
To cover the dry cleaning.

67
00:03:03,776 --> 00:03:06,483
Keep your strength up, future detective.

68
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:10,616
Thirty thousand won,
including the boiled pork? Alright.

69
00:03:10,616 --> 00:03:12,316
What's with her?

70
00:03:19,183 --> 00:03:22,216
[Episode 10]

71
00:03:22,216 --> 00:03:24,216
[Client Suitability Assessment,
One-Month Post-Release Observation]

72
00:03:24,216 --> 00:03:26,346
[Multiple Risk Indicators,
High Reoffending Risk]

73
00:03:34,368 --> 00:03:37,549
Why? Because of the victim's son who's a cop?

74
00:03:42,304 --> 00:03:45,976
I thought he looked familiar. Now I remember.

75
00:03:45,976 --> 00:03:51,176
I saw him in the first-floor lobby
when we were leaving your housewarming party.

76
00:03:51,176 --> 00:03:53,352
I've heard about it.

77
00:03:53,352 --> 00:03:55,128
He's a friend of my husband's.

78
00:03:55,128 --> 00:03:56,412
Yeah?

79
00:03:56,412 --> 00:03:58,112
Your husband...

80
00:03:59,136 --> 00:04:01,483
had a friend like that?

81
00:04:02,176 --> 00:04:07,283
If you're really uncomfortable with it,
let's change the scenario.

82
00:04:13,483 --> 00:04:16,332
Why do people never really change?

83
00:04:16,332 --> 00:04:19,000
Twenty years is a pretty long time.

84
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,700
Exactly.

85
00:04:21,668 --> 00:04:23,816
They commit sins
that even repentance and remorse

86
00:04:23,816 --> 00:04:26,796
can never make the victims' families forgive.

87
00:04:26,796 --> 00:04:28,448
Why do they even do it?

88
00:04:28,448 --> 00:04:30,183
At times like this,

89
00:04:30,816 --> 00:04:36,316
that saying, "A leopard can't change
its spots," feels so cruel, doesn't it?

90
00:04:36,316 --> 00:04:40,552
But still, not everyone kills just because

91
00:04:40,552 --> 00:04:42,883
they grew up in different
conditions and environments.

92
00:04:42,883 --> 00:04:49,359
Plenty of people serve the time they deserve
and then go on to live new lives.

93
00:04:50,116 --> 00:04:54,283
That's why the law and the state
give them another chance.

94
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,083
Let's stick to the scenario.

95
00:05:00,780 --> 00:05:02,483
Will you be okay?

96
00:05:03,166 --> 00:05:04,166
I have to be.

97
00:05:04,166 --> 00:05:08,349
It's my job, and it's what I can do.

98
00:05:21,292 --> 00:05:22,983
<i>Why are you going after that punk, you idiot?</i>

99
00:05:22,983 --> 00:05:25,916
What are you planning to do if you meet him?

100
00:05:26,664 --> 00:05:29,632
What do you mean? I'm just watching him.

101
00:05:29,632 --> 00:05:31,280
Why? What...

102
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:33,316
Worried the cop might do something reckless?

103
00:05:33,316 --> 00:05:34,968
Especially since I have a gun?

104
00:05:34,968 --> 00:05:37,896
Jeez, even your jokes are messed up.

105
00:05:37,896 --> 00:05:40,188
- Why do you have a gun...
- <i>If you know I'm joking,</i>

106
00:05:40,188 --> 00:05:42,828
stop worrying and go home.

107
00:05:42,828 --> 00:05:44,608
Didn't you say
your wife's working late tonight?

108
00:05:44,608 --> 00:05:46,308
<i>I'm hanging up.</i>

109
00:06:07,683 --> 00:06:08,880
[My Santa]

110
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,544
<i>I'm working late.</i>

111
00:06:10,544 --> 00:06:12,076
<i>Where are you, Tae Seong?</i>

112
00:06:12,076 --> 00:06:13,549
<i>I'm leaving work now.</i>

113
00:06:13,549 --> 00:06:17,212
<i>Se Ah said she'd watch Yul until eight.
I'll make sure I get home before then.</i>

114
00:06:17,212 --> 00:06:19,380
<i>I won't be too late either.</i>

115
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:20,583
<i>I'll call you when I'm done.</i>

116
00:06:20,583 --> 00:06:23,340
[Wednesday, May 6]

117
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:25,848
<i>Jang Eun Hak is leaving work.</i>

118
00:06:25,848 --> 00:06:28,232
He's expected to arrive in
about five minutes.

119
00:06:28,232 --> 00:06:29,932
<i>Okay.</i>

120
00:06:35,949 --> 00:06:38,216
He's entering the next block.

121
00:06:48,268 --> 00:06:51,783
Looks like he's buying something.
He just went into a convenience store.

122
00:06:52,928 --> 00:06:54,616
<i>Oh...</i>

123
00:06:54,616 --> 00:06:56,500
It's liquor.

124
00:06:56,500 --> 00:07:00,956
He grabbed a few bottles of soju
and sat down outside the store.

125
00:07:00,956 --> 00:07:02,883
<i>This could take a while.</i>

126
00:07:11,668 --> 00:07:16,284
Ms. Yoo, there's a man tailing Jang Eun Hak.

127
00:07:16,284 --> 00:07:17,975
- A man?
- <i>Looks like he's been following him</i>

128
00:07:17,975 --> 00:07:19,097
<i>since the workshop.</i>

129
00:07:19,097 --> 00:07:21,768
He's watching him from a distance.

130
00:07:21,768 --> 00:07:23,308
What does he look like?

131
00:07:23,308 --> 00:07:26,296
Wearing a jacket, mid-thirties, maybe?

132
00:07:26,296 --> 00:07:29,828
I can't make out his face on camera.

133
00:07:29,828 --> 00:07:31,549
Let me take a look.

134
00:07:54,532 --> 00:07:57,428
Could it be the son who's a cop...

135
00:07:57,428 --> 00:07:59,036
Yeah, that's him.

136
00:07:59,036 --> 00:08:00,849
Then I guess today...

137
00:08:02,088 --> 00:08:04,016
Let's just watch for now.

138
00:08:17,816 --> 00:08:19,716
Jang Eun Hak is moving.

139
00:08:20,636 --> 00:08:23,292
He's heading back the way he came?

140
00:08:23,292 --> 00:08:24,992
I see him.

141
00:08:42,852 --> 00:08:45,249
Jang Eun Hak has gone back into the workshop.

142
00:08:53,056 --> 00:08:56,452
Ms. Yoo, Jang Eun Hak made a move again.

143
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:58,983
What? What about the son?

144
00:09:00,144 --> 00:09:01,844
What? Is he hurt?

145
00:09:03,776 --> 00:09:06,112
<i>Jang Eun Hak bolted out.</i>

146
00:09:06,112 --> 00:09:08,716
<i>The son chased right after him.</i>

147
00:09:08,716 --> 00:09:10,849
[Dongwoon Furniture]
He's holding a gun.

148
00:09:28,556 --> 00:09:29,632
I'm heading out.

149
00:09:29,632 --> 00:09:31,516
<i>Track their route and keep me posted.</i>

150
00:09:31,516 --> 00:09:35,476
Ms. Yoo, Kwon Tae Seong is here.

151
00:09:35,476 --> 00:09:36,880
- What?
- <i>He went into the workshop,</i>

152
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:40,583
came back out, and ran off
in the direction the two of them went.

153
00:09:40,583 --> 00:09:42,468
Why is your husband here...

154
00:09:42,468 --> 00:09:45,252
Ms. Yoo! Ms. Yoo, are you listening?

155
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:46,644
Yeah, I'm listening.

156
00:09:46,644 --> 00:09:48,592
- Then let's pull out for today...
- No.

157
00:09:48,592 --> 00:09:49,952
<i>If we leave now, we'll lose him.</i>

158
00:09:49,952 --> 00:09:51,652
Keep going.

159
00:09:54,988 --> 00:09:56,488
I'm down. Which way?

160
00:09:56,488 --> 00:09:58,283
<i>Ms. Yoo, what are you going to do?</i>

161
00:09:58,283 --> 00:09:59,676
What if something happens today...

162
00:09:59,676 --> 00:10:01,376
<i>Ki Yeong Do.</i>

163
00:10:05,983 --> 00:10:07,783
With your back to the workshop,
you are on the left.

164
00:10:07,783 --> 00:10:10,756
<i>It's to your right, Ms. Yoo.</i>

165
00:10:10,756 --> 00:10:13,083
Don't take any unnecessary risks.

166
00:11:05,124 --> 00:11:07,149
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

167
00:11:26,976 --> 00:11:28,816
Jang Eun Hak, stop!

168
00:11:45,988 --> 00:11:47,688
Meeting concluded.

169
00:11:49,428 --> 00:11:51,776
Good work, Ms. Yoo.

170
00:11:51,776 --> 00:11:54,460
You should get out of there for now.

171
00:11:54,460 --> 00:11:56,160
Dong Jin!

172
00:12:05,692 --> 00:12:06,749
What's wrong with you?

173
00:12:06,749 --> 00:12:08,449
Are you okay?

174
00:12:09,652 --> 00:12:11,352
No...

175
00:12:12,072 --> 00:12:14,152
Not me. I didn't shoot him.

176
00:12:14,152 --> 00:12:18,252
- I know, I know.
- Not me... I...

177
00:12:22,488 --> 00:12:24,188
Kingfisher...

178
00:12:26,692 --> 00:12:28,600
Kingfisher was here.

179
00:12:28,600 --> 00:12:30,164
Kingfisher was here... Kingfisher...

180
00:12:30,164 --> 00:12:32,092
Kingfisher... Kingfisher...

181
00:12:32,092 --> 00:12:34,076
Kingfisher...

182
00:12:34,076 --> 00:12:36,783
Dong Jin!

183
00:12:37,549 --> 00:12:38,549
Dong Jin!

184
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:40,283
No.

185
00:12:40,916 --> 00:12:42,283
You need to get to a hospital first.

186
00:12:42,283 --> 00:12:43,983
You're hurt right now.

187
00:12:43,983 --> 00:12:45,716
I have to catch him.
I have to catch Kingfisher.

188
00:12:45,716 --> 00:12:48,424
You're bleeding badly now!

189
00:12:48,424 --> 00:12:49,632
He was here.

190
00:12:49,632 --> 00:12:52,149
Kingfisher was right here moments ago.

191
00:12:52,149 --> 00:12:54,949
Lee Dong Jin, Lee Dong Jin.

192
00:12:55,572 --> 00:12:56,900
Pull yourself together.

193
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:58,649
You have to stay conscious.

194
00:13:00,784 --> 00:13:02,484
Tae Seong.

195
00:13:05,608 --> 00:13:07,749
That punk, Jang Eun Hak...

196
00:13:10,904 --> 00:13:12,604
is dead.

197
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:15,416
That punk...

198
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:20,916
He is dead, that punk...

199
00:13:20,916 --> 00:13:25,083
Tae Seong, what do I do? I'm...

200
00:13:27,744 --> 00:13:30,083
I'm so glad that...

201
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,183
Jang Eun Hak is dead.

202
00:13:35,888 --> 00:13:37,588
And...

203
00:13:39,184 --> 00:13:41,552
I'm ashamed of myself for feeling that way.

204
00:13:41,552 --> 00:13:42,904
Dong Jin, it's alright.

205
00:13:42,904 --> 00:13:46,149
Dong Jin, it's alright. It's alright.

206
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:53,216
I was the person in the world
who wanted Jang Eun Hak dead the most.

207
00:13:54,496 --> 00:14:00,140
Every single day, without fail,
I wanted to kill him.

208
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:03,583
Even after twenty years,
whenever I think about that day...

209
00:14:12,484 --> 00:14:15,949
I imagined shooting him over and over again.

210
00:14:16,648 --> 00:14:21,049
I imagined a hole blown through his head,
his entire body torn to shreds,

211
00:14:22,520 --> 00:14:26,575
writhing in agony, then falling into hell.

212
00:14:26,575 --> 00:14:29,150
I wanted desperately to see it
with my own eyes.

213
00:14:29,150 --> 00:14:31,040
I know. I know, Dong Jin.

214
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:34,132
But first, let's go to the hospital. Please.

215
00:14:34,132 --> 00:14:36,183
Dong Jin, Dong Jin.

216
00:14:36,183 --> 00:14:38,156
You need to go to the hospital first.

217
00:14:38,156 --> 00:14:40,183
I have to catch Kingfisher.

218
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:43,652
He killed that punk!

219
00:14:43,652 --> 00:14:46,049
Kingfisher killed that punk.

220
00:14:46,049 --> 00:14:48,581
For twenty years you pictured it
over and over, but couldn't do it.

221
00:14:48,581 --> 00:14:50,616
Kingfisher did.

222
00:14:50,616 --> 00:14:52,083
You saw it, right?

223
00:14:52,083 --> 00:14:55,756
That punk was trying to kill someone again.

224
00:14:55,756 --> 00:14:58,556
That's right. I couldn't do it.

225
00:14:58,556 --> 00:15:01,048
Even when Jang Eun Hak
was running right in front of me,

226
00:15:01,048 --> 00:15:04,383
with the back of his head
right there in front of me,

227
00:15:05,349 --> 00:15:07,116
I still couldn't kill him.

228
00:15:07,116 --> 00:15:08,849
Do you know why?

229
00:15:11,092 --> 00:15:12,164
You asked me before.

230
00:15:12,164 --> 00:15:14,576
What if he didn't change?

231
00:15:14,576 --> 00:15:16,704
But I already had my answer.

232
00:15:16,704 --> 00:15:19,632
If he commits a crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in.

233
00:15:19,632 --> 00:15:21,996
If he gets out and commits another crime,
I'll catch him and throw him in again.

234
00:15:21,996 --> 00:15:23,416
I'll keep catching him and locking him up.

235
00:15:23,416 --> 00:15:26,032
That's my way,
and it's the right thing to do.

236
00:15:26,032 --> 00:15:30,564
No, in reality, those punks never get judged.

237
00:15:30,564 --> 00:15:35,049
Dong Jin, the law isn't perfect.
And you know that, right?

238
00:15:35,049 --> 00:15:36,549
Oh, yeah?

239
00:15:36,549 --> 00:15:38,749
Then do whatever you want.

240
00:15:38,749 --> 00:15:41,288
I don't care whether the law
is perfect or not.

241
00:15:41,288 --> 00:15:43,628
To me, they're just the same punks
who killed people.

242
00:15:43,628 --> 00:15:46,016
And catching punks like that is my job.

243
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:51,096
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

244
00:15:51,096 --> 00:15:53,716
Write a story, cover a case, whatever.

245
00:15:53,716 --> 00:15:55,549
You're a reporter, right?

246
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,483
Beom, where are you?

247
00:16:17,584 --> 00:16:18,776
Beom.

248
00:16:18,776 --> 00:16:21,720
Comb through all the nearby CCTV footage
and track his escape route.

249
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:25,516
And collect every fingerprint, footprint,
and trace evidence around the rooftop.

250
00:16:25,516 --> 00:16:27,316
Okay.

251
00:16:42,124 --> 00:16:43,760
Se Ah.

252
00:16:43,760 --> 00:16:45,788
- Huh? Oh.
- Sorry for waking you.

253
00:16:45,788 --> 00:16:47,152
Bo Na, you're home?

254
00:16:47,152 --> 00:16:50,568
Well, Tae Seong called earlier
saying he'd be late,

255
00:16:50,568 --> 00:16:52,949
so I washed Yul and put her to bed
in the master bedroom.

256
00:16:52,949 --> 00:16:55,025
Sorry I'm late. Thank you.

257
00:16:55,025 --> 00:16:56,816
Go ahead and do what you need to do.

258
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:04,911
[My Santa]
<i>Something came up.</i>

259
00:17:04,911 --> 00:17:08,816
<i>I'll be really late tonight.
Don't wait up. Go to bed first.</i>

260
00:17:31,749 --> 00:17:33,912
[Did Kingfisher...]

261
00:17:33,912 --> 00:17:35,683
<i>Did Kingfisher...</i>

262
00:17:36,740 --> 00:17:38,516
<i>see me too?</i>

263
00:17:52,084 --> 00:17:54,616
<i>That man that day...</i>

264
00:17:55,476 --> 00:17:58,096
<i>Was he really Kingfisher?</i>

265
00:17:58,096 --> 00:18:00,649
<i>Goodnight, Tae Seong.</i>

266
00:18:06,152 --> 00:18:08,060
<i>Tae Seong.</i>

267
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:11,848
I'll do my job, so you do yours.

268
00:18:11,848 --> 00:18:13,649
<i>You're a reporter, right?</i>

269
00:18:15,283 --> 00:18:16,453
[Did Kingfisher see me too?]

270
00:18:16,453 --> 00:18:18,416
[That man that day...
Was he really Kingfisher?]

271
00:18:23,792 --> 00:18:26,784
<i>Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene.</i>

272
00:18:26,784 --> 00:18:28,916
<i>A supermarket murder convict died</i>

273
00:18:28,916 --> 00:18:32,396
<i>after being shot while fleeing
an attempted murder.</i>

274
00:18:32,396 --> 00:18:35,391
<i>Jang Eun Hak, previously imprisoned
for the murder of a supermarket couple</i>

275
00:18:35,391 --> 00:18:37,476
<i>in Gangmyeon-dong 20 years ago,</i>

276
00:18:37,476 --> 00:18:41,916
<i>died after attempting another murder
just one month after his release on parole.</i>

277
00:18:43,876 --> 00:18:45,373
[Unusual Alleyway Attack]
<i>Another Kingfisher incident</i>

278
00:18:45,373 --> 00:18:47,180
[Kingfisher Strikes Again Last Night]
<i>occurred last night.</i>

279
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:48,847
<i>The victim this time was Mr. Jang,</i>

280
00:18:48,847 --> 00:18:52,044
<i>who had brutally murdered
a supermarket-owning couple 20 years ago.</i>

281
00:18:52,044 --> 00:18:54,105
[Supermarket Murder Convict Shot Dead]
<i>He was sentenced to 16 years,</i>

282
00:18:54,105 --> 00:18:56,221
[While Fleeing After Attempted Murder]
<i>and died a month after being paroled,</i>

283
00:18:56,221 --> 00:18:57,612
[Supermarket Couple Murder Found Dead]
<i>a year before his full term,</i>

284
00:18:57,612 --> 00:18:59,012
[One Month After Parole]
<i>sending shock through the community.</i>

285
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:00,012
- <i>Moreover, this incident differs from</i>
- They say Kingfisher

286
00:19:00,012 --> 00:19:01,012
- <i>the previous ones,</i>
- struck again yesterday.

287
00:19:01,012 --> 00:19:02,012
- <i>which mainly occurred</i>
- Really?

288
00:19:02,012 --> 00:19:03,012
- <i>in enclosed, isolated spaces.</i>
- Kingfisher is awesome.

289
00:19:03,012 --> 00:19:05,196
<i>Unlike other Kingfisher cases,</i>

290
00:19:05,196 --> 00:19:08,649
<i>this one occurred in a residential alley,
making it highly unusual.</i>

291
00:19:08,649 --> 00:19:11,583
[Exclusive: Kingfisher Crime Scene]
<i>Shockingly, Mr. Jang was revealed</i>

292
00:19:11,583 --> 00:19:13,949
<i>to have attempted to murder his employer.</i>

293
00:19:13,949 --> 00:19:17,393
<i>Just one month after being paroled,
he had committed another attempted murder,</i>

294
00:19:17,393 --> 00:19:18,796
<i>this time as a flagrant offender.</i>

295
00:19:18,796 --> 00:19:21,904
<i>Furthermore, given the urgent situation
with the suspect on the run,</i>

296
00:19:21,904 --> 00:19:23,916
<i>it is speculated that Kingfisher
may have broken from his usual pattern</i>

297
00:19:23,916 --> 00:19:28,183
<i>and carried out the shooting
in a public place.</i>

298
00:19:29,284 --> 00:19:31,152
Mommy, where is Daddy?

299
00:19:31,152 --> 00:19:33,200
Why isn't Daddy waking up?

300
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,540
Dad? Let Daddy sleep a little longer.

301
00:19:36,540 --> 00:19:38,849
Is Daddy a sleepyhead?

302
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:43,216
Daddy worked late last night, so he's tired.

303
00:19:43,216 --> 00:19:44,848
What work?

304
00:19:44,848 --> 00:19:47,308
Writing articles?

305
00:19:47,308 --> 00:19:49,604
What is an article?

306
00:19:49,604 --> 00:19:53,244
An article is something
that tells people in the world

307
00:19:53,244 --> 00:19:58,984
what happened, why it happened,
and what to do now. That's what it does.

308
00:19:58,984 --> 00:20:00,648
Yul, you finished all of this, right?

309
00:20:00,648 --> 00:20:04,336
Oh? You did? Then let's have this.

310
00:20:04,336 --> 00:20:06,720
You said you want to be tall
like Mommy and Daddy, right?

311
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:08,749
Then you need to eat this
and grow big and tall.

312
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:10,616
Here, eat.

313
00:20:11,728 --> 00:20:13,228
Is it good?

314
00:20:13,228 --> 00:20:14,276
It is good!

315
00:20:14,276 --> 00:20:15,976
Yeah?

316
00:20:18,024 --> 00:20:19,216
Daddy!

317
00:20:19,216 --> 00:20:21,440
My little precious! Oh, my!

318
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,660
My treasure!

319
00:20:23,660 --> 00:20:25,468
Did you sleep well?

320
00:20:25,468 --> 00:20:26,783
You're already all dressed?

321
00:20:26,783 --> 00:20:30,483
Yeah. I'm dressed, and I ate this too.

322
00:20:30,483 --> 00:20:33,204
I'm going to be this tall, just like you.

323
00:20:33,204 --> 00:20:35,048
Wow, really? Good job.

324
00:20:35,048 --> 00:20:36,132
Sorry, I overslept.

325
00:20:36,132 --> 00:20:39,956
I will make it up to you tomorrow, okay?

326
00:20:39,956 --> 00:20:42,264
Oh, my.

327
00:20:42,264 --> 00:20:44,368
Why don't you sleep a little longer?
You're already up?

328
00:20:44,368 --> 00:20:46,316
I have to get to work.

329
00:20:50,728 --> 00:20:52,928
You must have been tired
from working late last night too,

330
00:20:52,928 --> 00:20:55,149
and you were probably super busy
all alone today.

331
00:21:00,728 --> 00:21:04,936
What? What's with that meaningful look
so early in the morning...

332
00:21:04,936 --> 00:21:05,936
No, it's not that.

333
00:21:05,936 --> 00:21:08,416
It's the look of someone gazing
at someone precious.

334
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:14,556
Go wash up. I'll make you some toast.

335
00:21:14,556 --> 00:21:16,372
Just a second.

336
00:21:16,372 --> 00:21:18,716
Let me recharge first.

337
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:21,440
Me too.

338
00:21:25,392 --> 00:21:27,116
Go wash up.

339
00:21:28,128 --> 00:21:30,616
I'm having two pieces of toast.

340
00:21:32,616 --> 00:21:35,383
[Resignation Letter]

341
00:21:36,784 --> 00:21:38,524
Are you threatening me now?

342
00:21:38,524 --> 00:21:41,196
Say it to my face.
Don't do this with a piece of paper.

343
00:21:41,196 --> 00:21:42,722
I know there's
a Kingfisher countermeasure meeting today,

344
00:21:42,722 --> 00:21:44,896
chaired by the Commissioner General.

345
00:21:44,896 --> 00:21:46,120
So what?

346
00:21:46,120 --> 00:21:47,520
How many times have chiefs had meetings?

347
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:48,972
Don't you know
those meetings are just for show?

348
00:21:48,972 --> 00:21:50,680
Then please make sure
this one isn't just for show.

349
00:21:50,680 --> 00:21:52,196
How exactly am I supposed to do that?

350
00:21:52,196 --> 00:21:54,556
What, you want me to put you in charge?

351
00:21:54,556 --> 00:21:55,620
Why would I?

352
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:57,449
This is my case.

353
00:21:58,176 --> 00:22:01,212
What were you doing yesterday,
and now you come here?

354
00:22:01,212 --> 00:22:04,120
You finally came face-to-face
with the man you wanted to catch so badly.

355
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:06,049
But why didn't you catch him?

356
00:22:06,952 --> 00:22:08,652
Jeez.

357
00:22:09,532 --> 00:22:12,520
Other stations asked me
whether you deliberately let him get away.

358
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:15,848
They think you were stalling to give the guy

359
00:22:15,848 --> 00:22:18,283
who took your revenge for you time to escape.

360
00:22:19,784 --> 00:22:21,880
If that's the case,

361
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:24,560
it'll be grounds for an investigation
and disciplinary action.

362
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:30,810
Including why you were lurking around
Jang Eun Hak at that time.

363
00:22:31,652 --> 00:22:34,249
You don't think this will come up
in today's meeting?

364
00:22:38,244 --> 00:22:41,668
Only you know the truth.

365
00:22:41,668 --> 00:22:42,908
I won't ask you about it.

366
00:22:42,908 --> 00:22:44,783
But you need to let it go too.

367
00:22:45,804 --> 00:22:50,880
If an investigation or disciplinary action
comes up, I'll cover for you.

368
00:22:50,880 --> 00:22:52,580
You can go now.

369
00:22:53,928 --> 00:22:56,600
I won't make excuses.
I'll take responsibility.

370
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,552
If they tell me to accept
the punishment, I will.

371
00:22:58,552 --> 00:23:00,336
If they give me a chance, I'll make it right.

372
00:23:00,336 --> 00:23:02,349
And if neither is possible...

373
00:23:02,349 --> 00:23:04,312
[Resignation Letter]

374
00:23:04,312 --> 00:23:06,528
Please accept my resignation.

375
00:23:06,528 --> 00:23:08,304
Hey, take this back.

376
00:23:08,304 --> 00:23:09,764
Hey, Lee Dong Jin.

377
00:23:09,764 --> 00:23:11,516
Hey, Dong Jin.

378
00:23:12,312 --> 00:23:15,749
Jeez, he's bowing, which he never does.

379
00:23:21,688 --> 00:23:23,772
Oh, Mr. Lee.

380
00:23:23,772 --> 00:23:26,408
As expected, all the CCTV footage
around the area was wiped.

381
00:23:26,408 --> 00:23:29,048
It was a no-parking zone, so there wasn't
anything useful from dashcams either.

382
00:23:29,048 --> 00:23:31,580
There's a public parking lot in the back.

383
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:32,580
I saw it.

384
00:23:32,580 --> 00:23:33,752
You did?

385
00:23:33,752 --> 00:23:36,576
Most of the people living there
work in the furniture district,

386
00:23:36,576 --> 00:23:39,516
so it's normally deserted at that hour
because everyone goes to bed early.

387
00:23:39,516 --> 00:23:42,449
Jeez, and no word on any witnesses, either.

388
00:23:43,300 --> 00:23:44,652
What about forensics?

389
00:23:44,652 --> 00:23:47,632
Nothing yet. Doesn't look like
they recovered much from the scene.

390
00:23:47,632 --> 00:23:50,300
But you never know what might turn up,
so keep checking regularly.

391
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:51,832
Okay.

392
00:23:51,832 --> 00:23:53,740
But are you okay, Mr. Lee?

393
00:23:53,740 --> 00:23:56,472
How do you think I feel after letting him
slip away right in front of me?

394
00:23:56,472 --> 00:23:57,876
No, I didn't mean that.

395
00:23:57,876 --> 00:24:00,816
The victim, Jang Eun Hak, is that person...

396
00:24:02,376 --> 00:24:04,444
Enough.

397
00:24:04,444 --> 00:24:07,672
What happened with those couple of
assault suspects from last time?

398
00:24:07,672 --> 00:24:09,648
Nothing yet on that one.

399
00:24:09,648 --> 00:24:11,883
The cybercrime unit
hasn't found anything either.

400
00:24:13,312 --> 00:24:16,056
So what are you going to do without me?

401
00:24:16,056 --> 00:24:18,476
What? Why would you be gone?

402
00:24:18,476 --> 00:24:20,176
Where are you going?

403
00:24:21,816 --> 00:24:23,492
[Civil Servant ID, Lee Dong Jin]

404
00:24:23,492 --> 00:24:25,084
You're getting a new mentor soon.

405
00:24:25,084 --> 00:24:29,449
Keep your eyes open
and learn everything you can.

406
00:24:30,888 --> 00:24:33,349
And don't make your previous mentor look bad.

407
00:24:37,356 --> 00:24:40,044
Wait, you're not quitting, are you?
You're not, right?

408
00:24:40,044 --> 00:24:42,000
Jeez, where are you going?

409
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:43,844
I'm going to sleep.

410
00:24:43,844 --> 00:24:45,383
Now of all times?

411
00:24:45,383 --> 00:24:47,549
[Investigative Reporting Team]

412
00:24:47,549 --> 00:24:48,649
[Kwon Tae Seong]

413
00:24:48,649 --> 00:24:50,316
[Kingfisher, Search Results]

414
00:24:50,316 --> 00:24:52,049
[Kingfisher: Notorious Killer
or Avenger of Justice?]

415
00:24:53,149 --> 00:24:54,149
An avenger of justice...

416
00:24:54,149 --> 00:24:55,930
[Reporter Kwon Tae Seong
tracked the cases involving Kingfisher]

417
00:24:55,930 --> 00:24:57,216
[and found what they had in common]

418
00:24:58,683 --> 00:25:00,349
[Five Reflections on Kingfisher]

419
00:25:00,349 --> 00:25:03,883
[The Painful Questions Kingfisher
Forces Our Society to Ask]

420
00:25:04,749 --> 00:25:07,083
[Even if Kingfisher is caught tomorrow,
the questions he raised will remain]

421
00:25:07,083 --> 00:25:08,783
[Kwon Tae Seong, Social Affairs Reporter]

422
00:25:09,483 --> 00:25:11,768
Wow! As expected of Kwon Tae Seong.

423
00:25:11,768 --> 00:25:15,292
His comeback piece on Kingfisher
is an on-the-ground exclusive too.

424
00:25:15,292 --> 00:25:17,672
Ms. Gu, did you go there with him?

425
00:25:17,672 --> 00:25:20,764
Oh, no, I didn't know about it.

426
00:25:20,764 --> 00:25:23,888
Really? What? He acted like
he wasn't interested,

427
00:25:23,888 --> 00:25:26,260
but he was digging into it on his own?

428
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:28,176
So it was all an act.

429
00:25:28,176 --> 00:25:29,244
But why isn't he here?

430
00:25:29,244 --> 00:25:31,416
We need a follow-up article fast.

431
00:25:34,716 --> 00:25:37,436
<i>Let's focus on the parole system
for our next piece.</i>

432
00:25:37,436 --> 00:25:41,508
<i>Let's look into possible loopholes
in Jang Eun Hak's parole review process,</i>

433
00:25:41,508 --> 00:25:44,952
<i>and focus on preventive measures
so this kind of thing doesn't happen again.</i>

434
00:25:44,952 --> 00:25:47,704
<i>Based on your research,
prepare a draft article.</i>

435
00:25:47,704 --> 00:25:48,949
<i>I have somewhere else I need to go today.</i>

436
00:25:48,949 --> 00:25:50,080
What's he saying? Why isn't he coming?

437
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:52,900
Oh, I don't know about that.

438
00:25:52,900 --> 00:25:54,840
He just told me to prepare the article.

439
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:58,176
Oh! A quick follow-up story? I like it.

440
00:25:58,176 --> 00:25:59,876
What's the angle?

441
00:26:01,724 --> 00:26:05,548
The homework Kingfisher left us?

442
00:26:05,548 --> 00:26:08,404
Oh, homework?

443
00:26:08,404 --> 00:26:10,104
What's that supposed to mean?

444
00:26:17,404 --> 00:26:19,104
Director Yoo

445
00:26:19,716 --> 00:26:23,444
must have been quite surprised
by her husband's article.

446
00:26:23,444 --> 00:26:25,216
She knew about it.

447
00:26:26,140 --> 00:26:29,848
- What?
- She fired, knowing her husband was coming.

448
00:26:29,848 --> 00:26:35,724
She probably figured that if she missed
the shot, more people might get hurt.

449
00:26:35,724 --> 00:26:39,564
What if she bumped into her husband?

450
00:26:39,564 --> 00:26:41,916
She probably factored all of that
into her decision.

451
00:26:42,816 --> 00:26:45,583
Because she has never once been wrong.

452
00:26:46,588 --> 00:26:50,176
She's never been wrong. Never made a mistake.

453
00:26:50,176 --> 00:26:53,948
Anyway, Assistant Manager Ki,
you must've had a hard time.

454
00:26:53,948 --> 00:26:58,812
I erased what I could
and checked for witnesses and vehicles,

455
00:26:58,812 --> 00:27:03,224
but the area was huge,
so I'm not sure we covered every route.

456
00:27:03,224 --> 00:27:06,476
We didn't get a chance to check
the new sniper position afterward, either.

457
00:27:06,476 --> 00:27:09,068
Getting out quickly was our priority.

458
00:27:09,068 --> 00:27:11,420
So now,

459
00:27:11,420 --> 00:27:14,460
we don't know where something
could come from, huh?

460
00:27:14,460 --> 00:27:18,376
So far, nothing concerning
has appeared in the police database.

461
00:27:18,376 --> 00:27:20,916
Keep monitoring it closely.

462
00:27:21,660 --> 00:27:25,436
And for the time being,
let's leave out the sniper stuff.

463
00:27:25,436 --> 00:27:27,196
Understood.

464
00:27:27,196 --> 00:27:28,896
Good work.

465
00:27:35,096 --> 00:27:37,348
Let's give you a bath, Tae Soon.

466
00:27:37,348 --> 00:27:41,072
You'll start to smell
if you don't get washed regularly.

467
00:27:41,072 --> 00:27:45,992
Yoo Bo Na must have had a great time,
like flying high, right?

468
00:27:45,992 --> 00:27:47,883
Shall we wash your hair too?

469
00:27:52,356 --> 00:27:56,572
Ah, you're so pretty.

470
00:27:56,572 --> 00:27:59,749
Nice and cool.

471
00:28:18,724 --> 00:28:20,516
Wow, look at all this dust.

472
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:25,744
How can this be where our Director Yoo stays,
even for a minute?

473
00:28:25,744 --> 00:28:28,840
Jeez, move over there a bit!

474
00:28:28,840 --> 00:28:31,428
I'm going to get lung inflammation
from this, seriously.

475
00:28:31,428 --> 00:28:36,116
I can't sleep at night. I can't sleep.

476
00:28:37,888 --> 00:28:41,264
Our great Kingfisher
should be resting well today.

477
00:28:41,264 --> 00:28:44,188
But what is she doing?
Is she sleeping soundly?

478
00:28:44,188 --> 00:28:48,084
Even the way she sleeps must be totally cool.

479
00:28:48,084 --> 00:28:49,980
Oh, seriously, what are these?

480
00:28:49,980 --> 00:28:52,952
Keep this stuff cleaned up!

481
00:28:52,952 --> 00:28:54,949
Jeez.

482
00:28:54,949 --> 00:28:56,828
Ugh. What got on it, seriously?

483
00:28:56,828 --> 00:28:59,449
This is expensive,
and it can't even be dry-cleaned.

484
00:29:00,592 --> 00:29:03,084
How long has that trash been sitting here?

485
00:29:03,084 --> 00:29:05,916
Tae Soon, you got scared, didn't you?

486
00:29:07,649 --> 00:29:09,736
Are you really not going to help?

487
00:29:09,736 --> 00:29:11,436
Clean this up, now!

488
00:29:25,260 --> 00:29:27,588
Training's pretty intense today?

489
00:29:27,588 --> 00:29:30,316
You usually train like this
when you have a lot on your mind.

490
00:29:33,764 --> 00:29:36,580
I felt like my body was a bit stiff.

491
00:29:36,580 --> 00:29:40,149
Yesterday's mission was intense too.
You should get some rest.

492
00:29:44,308 --> 00:29:45,872
What about the shop?

493
00:29:45,872 --> 00:29:47,428
What if a customer comes?

494
00:29:47,428 --> 00:29:50,444
The only customers I have are flies.

495
00:29:50,444 --> 00:29:52,949
Guess I'll help you make a few more sales.

496
00:29:55,196 --> 00:29:58,216
Looks like your husband was at the scene.

497
00:29:59,780 --> 00:30:01,692
It's nothing you need to worry about.

498
00:30:01,692 --> 00:30:04,283
If it's work,
there's no reason for me to worry.

499
00:30:13,092 --> 00:30:15,528
Yul must have grown a lot lately.

500
00:30:15,528 --> 00:30:19,483
She's asking what her daddy does.

501
00:30:21,116 --> 00:30:26,616
I tell her, "Well, your daddy is someone
who does this kind of work."

502
00:30:29,149 --> 00:30:31,349
She may not understand now,

503
00:30:31,968 --> 00:30:34,248
but someday she will, right?

504
00:30:34,248 --> 00:30:36,728
What kind of person her daddy is.

505
00:30:36,728 --> 00:30:39,049
She'll be proud of him.

506
00:30:40,408 --> 00:30:43,749
That's the kind of work he does.

507
00:30:44,568 --> 00:30:47,183
It's when he's doing that work
that he really shines.

508
00:30:50,156 --> 00:30:55,583
He does his job, and I do mine.

509
00:30:57,332 --> 00:30:59,972
As for the unavoidable variables
that come up along the way...

510
00:30:59,972 --> 00:31:05,616
well, I'll manage them
just like I did in the field.

511
00:31:06,888 --> 00:31:09,368
Isn't that what you taught me?

512
00:31:09,368 --> 00:31:10,724
I did?

513
00:31:10,724 --> 00:31:15,383
Well, that was so long ago.
I barely remember.

514
00:31:21,192 --> 00:31:22,640
[Hye Ri's Mom]
<i>This is Hye Ri's mom.</i>

515
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,784
<i>You got the call from the daycare, right?</i>

516
00:31:24,784 --> 00:31:27,868
<i>Don't you think we need to talk?</i>

517
00:31:27,868 --> 00:31:31,316
Why? What's the problem this time?

518
00:31:31,316 --> 00:31:35,296
[Yul's Daycare]

519
00:31:35,296 --> 00:31:37,749
Yes, Miss.

520
00:31:37,749 --> 00:31:39,449
Yul?

521
00:31:41,972 --> 00:31:43,916
Oh...

522
00:31:43,916 --> 00:31:45,649
Really?

523
00:32:04,416 --> 00:32:08,032
<i>Assistant Manager Ki, this is Kwon Se Ah.</i>

524
00:32:08,032 --> 00:32:10,740
<i>I got your number from Bo Na
and wanted to reach out.</i>

525
00:32:10,740 --> 00:32:13,880
<i>I'd like to return your cleaned clothes.</i>

526
00:32:13,880 --> 00:32:17,716
<i>When would be convenient?</i>

527
00:32:20,832 --> 00:32:22,649
<i>Just throw them...</i>

528
00:32:36,740 --> 00:32:38,749
<i>Let's meet after work today.</i>

529
00:32:40,708 --> 00:32:42,588
Today!

530
00:32:42,588 --> 00:32:44,316
Yeah!

531
00:32:44,316 --> 00:32:47,320
Hey, Kwon Se Ah! You can do this, right?

532
00:32:47,320 --> 00:32:48,483
Today's the day!

533
00:32:48,483 --> 00:32:51,983
He said let's meet today,
not tomorrow. What do I do?

534
00:32:52,752 --> 00:32:53,883
Oh?

535
00:32:53,883 --> 00:32:55,683
Oh, jeez.

536
00:32:57,500 --> 00:32:58,836
[Mr. Tiger]
<i>What are you doing now?</i>

537
00:32:58,836 --> 00:33:01,060
<i>I'm a little down today.
Let's just grab a meal.</i>

538
00:33:01,060 --> 00:33:02,760
What?

539
00:33:07,212 --> 00:33:09,328
<i>The customer's phone is turned off...</i>

540
00:33:09,328 --> 00:33:14,183
Seriously, where is he hiding
with his phone turned off?

541
00:33:14,849 --> 00:33:18,108
Was the shock of missing
Kingfisher too much for him?

542
00:33:18,108 --> 00:33:19,683
He's not really quitting, is he?

543
00:33:19,683 --> 00:33:22,283
[You have a new message]

544
00:33:24,049 --> 00:33:26,249
<i>Eat by yourself. I'm busy.</i>

545
00:33:27,796 --> 00:33:30,872
<i>Another date today?
With your sister-in-law again?</i>

546
00:33:30,872 --> 00:33:32,408
<i>No. Today it's with a guy.</i>

547
00:33:32,408 --> 00:33:33,820
Oh, with a guy.

548
00:33:33,820 --> 00:33:36,504
W-W-With a guy?

549
00:33:36,504 --> 00:33:38,204
With who?

550
00:33:44,016 --> 00:33:47,949
Yul, did something happen at kindergarten?

551
00:33:48,764 --> 00:33:50,464
Look at Mommy.

552
00:33:55,536 --> 00:33:58,764
Can you tell me what happened?

553
00:33:58,764 --> 00:34:01,576
That way, I can help you.

554
00:34:01,576 --> 00:34:05,740
Yul, I'm your best friend, remember?

555
00:34:05,740 --> 00:34:08,916
Best friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

556
00:34:10,068 --> 00:34:13,616
Mommy...

557
00:34:14,340 --> 00:34:15,968
Mommy.

558
00:34:15,968 --> 00:34:17,160
Oh, I see.

559
00:34:17,160 --> 00:34:19,920
Were you upset?

560
00:34:19,920 --> 00:34:22,916
Oh, dear. You were upset? Okay.

561
00:34:22,916 --> 00:34:25,449
I'm sorry. I understand.

562
00:34:28,356 --> 00:34:30,349
Mommy.

563
00:35:09,448 --> 00:35:13,249
<i>A punk who shot a dad dead</i>

564
00:35:14,132 --> 00:35:17,128
<i>right in front of his seven-year-old son.</i>

565
00:35:17,128 --> 00:35:22,424
<i>The kid was so traumatized
that he still can't speak.</i>

566
00:35:22,424 --> 00:35:27,904
A normal human being
wouldn't kill a parent in front of a child.

567
00:35:27,904 --> 00:35:32,316
No matter how vile the criminal was,
that still isn't right, right?

568
00:35:42,776 --> 00:35:45,160
What is it? What do you want?

569
00:35:45,160 --> 00:35:49,244
Does an elderly lady
and her grandson live here?

570
00:35:49,244 --> 00:35:50,949
An elderly lady?

571
00:35:51,644 --> 00:35:55,032
Oh, you must mean the people
who lived here before.

572
00:35:55,032 --> 00:35:57,683
I moved in last year.

573
00:35:59,252 --> 00:36:01,149
Okay, I see.

574
00:36:01,149 --> 00:36:02,868
[Ongsan Dream Real Estate]
Oh, that old lady?

575
00:36:02,868 --> 00:36:05,342
- She went to a nursing home last year.
- A nursing home?

576
00:36:05,342 --> 00:36:08,176
She had dementia or something
starting a few years ago.

577
00:36:08,176 --> 00:36:11,524
She's probably been a bit
in and out of it mentally for a while.

578
00:36:11,524 --> 00:36:15,404
Then what about the kid...
She had a grandson, didn't she?

579
00:36:15,404 --> 00:36:17,004
Her grandson?

580
00:36:17,004 --> 00:36:20,540
Oh, the boy who spoke strangely
and barely talked?

581
00:36:20,540 --> 00:36:25,484
Yeah. He'd been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

582
00:36:25,484 --> 00:36:27,816
Do you happen to know where he is now?

583
00:36:27,816 --> 00:36:29,856
Didn't he end up in some kind of institution?

584
00:36:29,856 --> 00:36:31,376
Yeah, that's right.

585
00:36:31,376 --> 00:36:35,549
There was no one to take care of him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.

586
00:36:37,528 --> 00:36:39,272
Here.

587
00:36:39,272 --> 00:36:41,976
Sorry I'm returning these so late,
Assistant Manager Ki.

588
00:36:41,976 --> 00:36:44,483
They've been cleaned for a while,

589
00:36:44,483 --> 00:36:48,236
but I wasn't sure
how to get them back to you.

590
00:36:48,236 --> 00:36:49,936
Okay.

591
00:36:51,072 --> 00:36:52,772
Yeah.

592
00:36:54,628 --> 00:36:55,928
Don't you have anything else to say?

593
00:36:55,928 --> 00:36:57,480
Pardon?

594
00:36:57,480 --> 00:37:01,149
Oh, I guess it's my turn to talk.

595
00:37:02,016 --> 00:37:04,383
I believe we had a date planned.

596
00:37:06,888 --> 00:37:10,000
Oh, you remember.

597
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:13,464
Then shall we start with dinner?

598
00:37:13,464 --> 00:37:15,164
I'm fine without eating.

599
00:37:21,088 --> 00:37:23,068
Hey, what are you doing here?

600
00:37:23,068 --> 00:37:25,672
You! Why are you here?
How did you know I was here?

601
00:37:25,672 --> 00:37:26,683
You told me.

602
00:37:26,683 --> 00:37:27,683
Huh?

603
00:37:27,683 --> 00:37:30,583
"Hey, where are you?" "Me? Yun Cafe."

604
00:37:30,583 --> 00:37:32,084
I've been looking everywhere for you.

605
00:37:32,084 --> 00:37:33,992
Why?

606
00:37:33,992 --> 00:37:36,948
Hello. I'm Beom Seong Hun,
Se Dol's friend here.

607
00:37:36,948 --> 00:37:38,144
I've heard a lot about you.

608
00:37:38,144 --> 00:37:40,249
Hey, what have I even said about him...

609
00:37:40,249 --> 00:37:41,249
No, I didn't.

610
00:37:41,249 --> 00:37:42,664
If it's not rude, may I join you?

611
00:37:42,664 --> 00:37:46,008
No, it is rude. It's very rude.
You're being incredibly rude.

612
00:37:46,008 --> 00:37:49,968
Oh, he might seem a bit clueless,
but he's definitely not a bad guy.

613
00:37:49,968 --> 00:37:52,952
First of all, his job is a cop.

614
00:37:52,952 --> 00:37:55,449
Can't you see this isn't exactly
the place for you right now?

615
00:37:55,449 --> 00:37:58,676
Why don't you leave while I'm asking nicely?

616
00:37:58,676 --> 00:38:01,052
Hey, why isn't this the place for me?

617
00:38:01,052 --> 00:38:02,692
Don't you know the world is
a dangerous place these days?

618
00:38:02,692 --> 00:38:04,005
Even if he looks innocent on the outside,

619
00:38:04,005 --> 00:38:07,350
an expert like me needs to scan him
and see if he's rotten on the inside.

620
00:38:07,350 --> 00:38:08,883
You, seriously...

621
00:38:09,880 --> 00:38:13,804
Not that I'm saying that's what you are,
of course. Don't get me wrong.

622
00:38:13,804 --> 00:38:17,449
We were just about to
go get something to eat.

623
00:38:18,404 --> 00:38:20,744
Shall we get going?

624
00:38:20,744 --> 00:38:21,936
Oh, food!

625
00:38:21,936 --> 00:38:23,083
Hey, perfect timing.

626
00:38:23,083 --> 00:38:25,372
I was just getting hungry.

627
00:38:25,372 --> 00:38:28,516
Well, since we've met like this,
why don't we have a meal together?

628
00:38:28,516 --> 00:38:29,696
I know a good place nearby.

629
00:38:29,696 --> 00:38:33,412
Assistant Manager Ki, we'll go ahead.
Can you come out in a little while?

630
00:38:33,412 --> 00:38:34,836
Sure.

631
00:38:34,836 --> 00:38:36,549
- Come on out!
- Hey.

632
00:38:39,556 --> 00:38:40,636
Oh, seriously.

633
00:38:40,636 --> 00:38:43,864
Hey, put this down.

634
00:38:43,864 --> 00:38:45,744
Hey, do you have a gun on you right now?

635
00:38:45,744 --> 00:38:47,208
Do you think I would? What's with the gun?

636
00:38:47,208 --> 00:38:49,283
So I can blow your head off!

637
00:38:49,283 --> 00:38:51,183
Hey, that hurts!

638
00:38:51,956 --> 00:38:53,008
I came because I was worried about you, okay?

639
00:38:53,008 --> 00:38:55,116
About what?

640
00:38:55,116 --> 00:38:57,064
You know I've got good instincts, right?

641
00:38:57,064 --> 00:38:59,576
Oh, you do? You do?

642
00:38:59,576 --> 00:39:02,449
There's something off about that guy.

643
00:39:02,449 --> 00:39:04,588
Like he reeks of a brutal crime or something?

644
00:39:04,588 --> 00:39:06,783
He's my sister-in-law's coworker, got it?

645
00:39:07,988 --> 00:39:11,716
Then that whole company sounds suspicious.

646
00:39:11,716 --> 00:39:13,264
Hmm...

647
00:39:13,264 --> 00:39:15,684
If you don't have a gun,
I'll use my bare hands, you punk!

648
00:39:15,684 --> 00:39:17,316
Why did you come here? Aren't you leaving?

649
00:39:17,316 --> 00:39:20,049
Why'd you come here just to piss me off?

650
00:39:20,049 --> 00:39:22,316
- Hey, that's enough.
- Where is it?

651
00:39:23,684 --> 00:39:25,012
That restaurant.

652
00:39:25,012 --> 00:39:26,712
What?

653
00:39:33,516 --> 00:39:37,140
This is the kind of chicken feet place
you can't quit once you've tried it.

654
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:39,893
Alright, starting with
whole chicken feet, spicy chicken feet,

655
00:39:39,893 --> 00:39:41,292
boneless chicken feet,
and braised chicken feet.

656
00:39:41,292 --> 00:39:43,764
For the record, our usual move
is to start with the soupy ones

657
00:39:43,764 --> 00:39:45,683
and finish with the grilled spicy ones.

658
00:39:45,683 --> 00:39:47,236
Do you like chicken feet?

659
00:39:47,236 --> 00:39:49,583
Sometimes. Very occasionally.

660
00:39:49,583 --> 00:39:52,583
They're also packed with collagen, you know.

661
00:39:56,024 --> 00:39:57,168
Can't you eat them?

662
00:39:57,168 --> 00:40:00,783
No. I'm going to give them
a try starting today.

663
00:40:00,783 --> 00:40:02,583
Then please enjoy.

664
00:40:12,284 --> 00:40:13,984
Cheers!

665
00:40:17,672 --> 00:40:19,372
Cheers!

666
00:40:22,088 --> 00:40:23,224
This is so good.

667
00:40:23,224 --> 00:40:26,349
You said you're a cop. What division?

668
00:40:27,444 --> 00:40:29,449
Criminal Affairs, Violent Crimes.

669
00:40:30,176 --> 00:40:32,448
Oh, Violent Crimes.

670
00:40:32,448 --> 00:40:35,516
You must get some interesting cases.

671
00:40:35,516 --> 00:40:37,164
Plenty of horrible ones.

672
00:40:37,164 --> 00:40:39,356
People die, get hurt, get messed up.

673
00:40:39,356 --> 00:40:42,316
What case have you been working on lately?

674
00:40:44,116 --> 00:40:46,328
That's confidential.

675
00:40:46,328 --> 00:40:50,616
You seem really interested in crime, though?

676
00:40:51,660 --> 00:40:53,864
I'm interested in profiling.

677
00:40:53,864 --> 00:40:56,216
I majored in psychology too.

678
00:40:57,249 --> 00:40:59,668
You majored in psychology.

679
00:40:59,668 --> 00:41:01,383
That's impressive.

680
00:41:02,036 --> 00:41:04,283
Then let me give you a scenario.

681
00:41:04,283 --> 00:41:06,849
Want to try profiling it for fun?

682
00:41:07,936 --> 00:41:10,052
Sounds fun.

683
00:41:10,052 --> 00:41:12,224
Okay, a man

684
00:41:12,224 --> 00:41:15,816
was shot dead through a gap
in a motel window by a sniper rifle.

685
00:41:16,488 --> 00:41:18,340
Who's the killer?

686
00:41:18,340 --> 00:41:20,464
Are you kidding? The whole country knows.

687
00:41:20,464 --> 00:41:21,600
It happened yesterday too.

688
00:41:21,600 --> 00:41:23,508
Hey, do you think I'd ask about that?

689
00:41:23,508 --> 00:41:27,016
Who do you think Kingfisher really is?

690
00:41:28,024 --> 00:41:29,724
I'm not sure.

691
00:41:30,796 --> 00:41:35,149
The police don't have enough evidence
to make an inference like that.

692
00:41:36,083 --> 00:41:41,000
The whole process is extremely methodical,
and he leaves no evidence behind.

693
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:44,183
That's why I have a theory.

694
00:41:44,183 --> 00:41:48,916
"Maybe Kingfisher isn't acting alone?"
That kind of.

695
00:41:50,696 --> 00:41:52,208
That's possible.

696
00:41:52,208 --> 00:41:54,616
His methods do seem highly organized.

697
00:41:55,844 --> 00:41:59,383
But you sound pretty certain, though?

698
00:42:01,576 --> 00:42:04,183
That he never leaves any evidence.

699
00:42:04,816 --> 00:42:07,149
That's why the police
haven't caught him yet, right?

700
00:42:07,848 --> 00:42:10,336
Ma'am, one more order of
chicken feet in broth, please.

701
00:42:10,336 --> 00:42:12,140
Yeah.

702
00:42:12,140 --> 00:42:13,483
Hey!

703
00:42:13,483 --> 00:42:15,604
Did you really eat all that
by yourself already?

704
00:42:15,604 --> 00:42:17,672
Me?

705
00:42:17,672 --> 00:42:19,372
Oh, my.

706
00:42:25,236 --> 00:42:27,949
Wait, you've got something on you.

707
00:42:38,284 --> 00:42:40,592
Thank you.

708
00:42:40,592 --> 00:42:43,049
It's nice to see someone
with such a good appetite.

709
00:42:46,183 --> 00:42:49,416
I usually eat pretty well.

710
00:42:49,416 --> 00:42:51,783
Assistant Manager Ki,
you should eat some too.

711
00:42:51,783 --> 00:42:54,872
Oh, I'm fine. I don't really eat that much.

712
00:42:54,872 --> 00:42:55,996
Oh, right.

713
00:42:55,996 --> 00:42:58,616
You did say you don't eat much, right?

714
00:42:59,496 --> 00:43:01,272
I should get going.

715
00:43:01,272 --> 00:43:02,449
I need to head back to the station.

716
00:43:02,449 --> 00:43:03,724
Yeah? You sure?

717
00:43:03,724 --> 00:43:05,372
Go ahead, bye.

718
00:43:05,372 --> 00:43:07,212
Don't forget to pay on your way out.

719
00:43:07,212 --> 00:43:09,564
Yeah, just stay and have some fun.

720
00:43:09,564 --> 00:43:12,116
Maybe we'll see each other again sometime.

721
00:43:25,392 --> 00:43:29,016
Wow! Looks like Se Dol
finally escaped the single life.

722
00:43:30,580 --> 00:43:33,783
Jeez, but why do I feel like this?

723
00:43:39,896 --> 00:43:43,049
Wow, one beer here costs...

724
00:43:43,049 --> 00:43:45,083
Is this some fancy place?

725
00:43:45,732 --> 00:43:48,683
Everyone, let's be prepared.

726
00:43:48,683 --> 00:43:52,149
We need to nip this in the bud.

727
00:43:58,804 --> 00:44:01,148
Both of you are here as well.

728
00:44:01,148 --> 00:44:03,449
Thanks for showing up.

729
00:44:05,384 --> 00:44:08,056
This isn't just about Hye Ri.

730
00:44:08,056 --> 00:44:13,004
Who knows whose child could be next?

731
00:44:13,004 --> 00:44:16,283
I ordered some beer and snacks. Is beer okay?

732
00:44:16,283 --> 00:44:19,088
Oh, absolutely. Beer sounds great.

733
00:44:19,088 --> 00:44:23,296
Well, since we're at a bar,
we might as well have a drink.

734
00:44:23,296 --> 00:44:25,360
What are you talking about, beer?

735
00:44:25,360 --> 00:44:28,644
We left the kids at home,
so let's keep this short and wrap it up.

736
00:44:28,644 --> 00:44:33,400
Just because of some stupid blocks,
those two kids ganged up and hurt Hye Ri.

737
00:44:33,400 --> 00:44:36,232
She must've been so upset.

738
00:44:36,232 --> 00:44:39,016
She came home and wouldn't even
eat her favorite pork cutlet...

739
00:44:40,804 --> 00:44:42,340
Oh, my.

740
00:44:42,340 --> 00:44:44,980
What's this?

741
00:44:44,980 --> 00:44:47,783
Is that Yul's finger?

742
00:44:48,692 --> 00:44:51,040
Oh, my God. What happened?

743
00:44:51,040 --> 00:44:53,432
Every time Seo Jun built something
with the blocks,

744
00:44:53,432 --> 00:44:54,948
Hye Ri would come and knock it down.

745
00:44:54,948 --> 00:44:58,383
So Yul tried to stop her.

746
00:44:58,383 --> 00:45:02,616
Then Hye Ri bit Yul's finger.

747
00:45:03,732 --> 00:45:07,752
Seo Jun got scared and pushed Hye Ri away.

748
00:45:07,752 --> 00:45:10,520
As far as he's concerned,
he was only trying to separate them.

749
00:45:10,520 --> 00:45:14,408
Wait, Hye Ri bit Yul?

750
00:45:14,408 --> 00:45:16,036
Hye Ri didn't mention any of that.

751
00:45:16,036 --> 00:45:20,680
Oh, maybe she was afraid you'd scold her,
so she didn't tell you.

752
00:45:20,680 --> 00:45:23,504
Oh, that must've hurt.

753
00:45:23,504 --> 00:45:28,683
Why didn't Yul tell the teacher about this?

754
00:45:30,304 --> 00:45:31,304
Wait.

755
00:45:31,304 --> 00:45:34,968
So did you call us here
to complain about this?

756
00:45:34,968 --> 00:45:37,416
To get an apology out of me?

757
00:45:38,452 --> 00:45:40,683
Hye Ri's mom.

758
00:45:40,683 --> 00:45:42,183
Yeah?

759
00:45:42,183 --> 00:45:45,816
No, why? What is it?

760
00:45:46,820 --> 00:45:52,083
As a mom, what am I supposed
to do in a situation like this...

761
00:45:53,356 --> 00:45:55,512
I honestly don't know.

762
00:45:55,512 --> 00:45:59,283
So I just told Yul what felt right to me.

763
00:45:59,283 --> 00:46:01,277
I told Yul that Hye Ri didn't do it
because she hated Yul.

764
00:46:01,277 --> 00:46:03,983
She was probably just upset for a moment.

765
00:46:09,008 --> 00:46:13,136
Well, the kids still have to
live together going forward.

766
00:46:13,136 --> 00:46:15,632
We need to comfort them
so this doesn't leave a bad memory,

767
00:46:15,632 --> 00:46:20,482
and help them get along better from now on.

768
00:46:20,482 --> 00:46:24,949
I think that's what adults should do.

769
00:46:25,568 --> 00:46:30,892
So I wanted to ask for your advice
on how to do that.

770
00:46:30,892 --> 00:46:32,656
Oh, what is there to do?

771
00:46:32,656 --> 00:46:35,816
Just discipline them
if they did something wrong,

772
00:46:35,816 --> 00:46:40,912
have them apologize if they need to,
and let the moms clear the air. That's all.

773
00:46:40,912 --> 00:46:42,381
- That's right.
- Yeah.

774
00:46:42,381 --> 00:46:44,312
Right.

775
00:46:44,312 --> 00:46:46,649
Oh, the drinks are here.

776
00:46:50,700 --> 00:46:52,400
Thank you.

777
00:46:53,764 --> 00:46:56,332
Oh, you made it?

778
00:46:56,332 --> 00:46:58,349
Sorry I'm late.

779
00:47:00,112 --> 00:47:02,080
Just a second.

780
00:47:02,080 --> 00:47:05,316
Oh, I saw some blood earlier,
and I'm still feeling queasy.

781
00:47:14,483 --> 00:47:16,368
Hye Ri's mom is...

782
00:47:16,368 --> 00:47:18,108
- Over here.
- Here.

783
00:47:18,108 --> 00:47:20,360
Oh, there you are.

784
00:47:20,360 --> 00:47:24,149
Hye Ri's mom, I heard
our Seo Jun pushed Hye Ri.

785
00:47:24,149 --> 00:47:27,156
That little punk.

786
00:47:27,156 --> 00:47:30,828
I'll give him a good talking-to
when I get home.

787
00:47:30,828 --> 00:47:33,000
I'll make him write an apology letter too.

788
00:47:33,000 --> 00:47:36,116
But I heard he already apologized to Hye Ri.

789
00:47:36,720 --> 00:47:38,272
Yes, he did.

790
00:47:38,272 --> 00:47:41,084
Yes, he apologized.

791
00:47:41,084 --> 00:47:42,916
Well, that's good.

792
00:47:44,492 --> 00:47:46,773
I'll apologize too, on behalf of his mom.

793
00:47:46,773 --> 00:47:49,183
- Well...
- I'm sorry, Hye Ri's mom.

794
00:47:50,212 --> 00:47:51,983
Wow!

795
00:47:51,983 --> 00:47:55,483
That's a bold apology.

796
00:48:01,094 --> 00:48:02,794
I...

797
00:48:05,476 --> 00:48:07,176
Sor...

798
00:48:08,528 --> 00:48:10,220
What should I do?

799
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:13,249
Do you think Yul will be okay
without going to the hospital?

800
00:48:15,956 --> 00:48:19,540
Oh, it went down pretty quickly
after I put some medicine on it.

801
00:48:19,540 --> 00:48:20,948
Thanks for asking.

802
00:48:20,948 --> 00:48:23,549
- Oh, good.
- What a relief.

803
00:48:24,688 --> 00:48:26,900
Wow, this is great, right?

804
00:48:26,900 --> 00:48:30,556
Let's have a proper drink
and loosen up. Cheers.

805
00:48:30,556 --> 00:48:32,300
- Out of drinks.
- Oh, no beer.

806
00:48:32,300 --> 00:48:33,672
Can I have a glass of beer?

807
00:48:33,672 --> 00:48:36,549
- Here, you can have some of mine for now.
- Okay, sure.

808
00:48:39,576 --> 00:48:41,184
Cheers.

809
00:48:41,184 --> 00:48:43,516
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

810
00:48:50,919 --> 00:48:52,300
Well...

811
00:48:52,300 --> 00:48:56,876
Assistant Manager Ki,
did I happen to do something wrong?

812
00:48:56,876 --> 00:48:58,576
Not at all.

813
00:48:59,432 --> 00:49:03,856
You just seem pretty different from
how you were at the restaurant.

814
00:49:03,856 --> 00:49:06,260
You haven't said much at all.

815
00:49:06,260 --> 00:49:08,928
This is the real me.
Earlier, I was putting on an act.

816
00:49:08,928 --> 00:49:11,500
Why would you do that?

817
00:49:11,500 --> 00:49:12,560
Do you like me?

818
00:49:12,560 --> 00:49:14,516
Yeah, I mean, no.

819
00:49:19,264 --> 00:49:20,600
Yeah.

820
00:49:20,600 --> 00:49:23,428
I'm sorry, but I have no interest in you.

821
00:49:23,428 --> 00:49:25,283
You're not my type.

822
00:49:26,112 --> 00:49:28,188
I'm sorry for asking you out.

823
00:49:28,188 --> 00:49:30,188
It was way too impulsive.

824
00:49:30,188 --> 00:49:32,076
Sorry.

825
00:49:32,076 --> 00:49:34,816
That's what I wanted to tell you,
so I asked to see you today.

826
00:49:37,984 --> 00:49:42,124
Then what is your type?

827
00:49:42,124 --> 00:49:43,824
I'm...

828
00:49:46,536 --> 00:49:49,616
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

829
00:49:49,616 --> 00:49:51,332
Eat up and relax, rookie.

830
00:49:51,332 --> 00:49:53,740
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

831
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:55,616
but chooses not to.

832
00:49:57,849 --> 00:50:01,149
That's quite a unique preference.

833
00:50:04,304 --> 00:50:08,088
But Assistant Manager Ki,
you don't even know me.

834
00:50:08,088 --> 00:50:10,060
That's right.

835
00:50:10,060 --> 00:50:12,383
And I don't particularly want to know you.

836
00:50:17,516 --> 00:50:19,148
Okay!

837
00:50:19,148 --> 00:50:21,949
Found today's punching bag.

838
00:50:21,949 --> 00:50:23,949
- Found one.
- Found one.

839
00:50:30,349 --> 00:50:32,649
[Cybercrime Unit, Sergeant Kim]

840
00:50:35,624 --> 00:50:37,888
- Yes, Mr. Kim.
- Hey, Mr. Beom. It's me.

841
00:50:37,888 --> 00:50:39,532
Guess what I found?

842
00:50:39,532 --> 00:50:40,949
I sent you a link.
Can you check it right away?

843
00:50:40,949 --> 00:50:43,649
Sure. Give me a second.

844
00:50:48,640 --> 00:50:50,883
<i>Hello, gentlemen!</i>

845
00:50:50,883 --> 00:50:53,583
- <i>It's time for Mace Man's justice.</i>
- <i>Justice!</i>

846
00:50:53,583 --> 00:50:56,564
<i>Let's get things started with a bang.</i>

847
00:50:56,564 --> 00:50:57,564
What's this?

848
00:50:57,564 --> 00:50:59,949
Apparently, it's a streaming site
that's been growing underground lately.

849
00:50:59,949 --> 00:51:02,712
They livestream violent or obscene videos,

850
00:51:02,712 --> 00:51:04,156
and apparently get paid in
some kind of cryptocurrency.

851
00:51:04,156 --> 00:51:08,736
<i>Who are we going to teach a lesson today?</i>

852
00:51:08,736 --> 00:51:10,316
<i>Let's go with a pretty one, if possible.</i>

853
00:51:10,316 --> 00:51:12,556
<i>You won't be able to see their faces
once they're covered in blood, idiot.</i>

854
00:51:12,556 --> 00:51:14,588
See them? Three masked men.

855
00:51:14,588 --> 00:51:17,736
These guys look like the couple-assault
suspects you've been after, right?

856
00:51:17,736 --> 00:51:20,316
Oh, you're right.

857
00:51:20,316 --> 00:51:23,432
Man, so cryptocurrency was their motive?

858
00:51:23,432 --> 00:51:24,640
Does it show where they are?

859
00:51:24,640 --> 00:51:25,924
It says Songju Park.

860
00:51:25,924 --> 00:51:27,220
Songju Park?

861
00:51:27,220 --> 00:51:28,749
Huh? That's nearby.

862
00:51:28,749 --> 00:51:32,044
<i>So what do you think of
these punks, gentlemen?</i>

863
00:51:32,044 --> 00:51:34,549
<i>Zoom in on the woman's face.</i>

864
00:51:34,549 --> 00:51:37,072
<i>Let's see.</i>

865
00:51:37,072 --> 00:51:39,284
- Huh?
- <i>There.</i>

866
00:51:39,284 --> 00:51:40,440
Darn it.

867
00:51:40,440 --> 00:51:42,140
Ah, well...

868
00:51:43,004 --> 00:51:45,696
Mr. Kim, please call for backup
from the local precinct,

869
00:51:45,696 --> 00:51:47,183
and send ambulances to Songju Park.

870
00:51:47,183 --> 00:51:48,652
- Three ambulances.
- Three?

871
00:51:48,652 --> 00:51:52,248
- Not two?
- No, three. Make sure it's three.

872
00:51:52,248 --> 00:51:55,404
No. Kwon Se Ah, please!

873
00:51:55,404 --> 00:51:57,104
This way, right?

874
00:51:57,724 --> 00:51:59,432
What are they doing?

875
00:51:59,432 --> 00:52:00,992
Why are they just walking?

876
00:52:00,992 --> 00:52:03,704
The guy's obviously a pathetic loser.

877
00:52:03,704 --> 00:52:06,172
He can't even hold her hand.

878
00:52:06,172 --> 00:52:12,049
Well, gentlemen,
I think it's time to teach them a lesson.

879
00:52:14,312 --> 00:52:15,777
I've already been rejected,

880
00:52:15,777 --> 00:52:18,649
but since I started this confession anyway,
let me just finish it.

881
00:52:19,944 --> 00:52:24,924
The first day we met,
when you said you'd help me find Yul,

882
00:52:24,924 --> 00:52:29,452
that's when you dove straight into my heart.

883
00:52:29,452 --> 00:52:31,152
And...

884
00:52:33,520 --> 00:52:35,220
Who on earth are you?

885
00:52:36,544 --> 00:52:38,244
Wait...

886
00:52:40,588 --> 00:52:43,016
Assistant Manager Ki, are you okay?

887
00:52:45,396 --> 00:52:47,216
<i>I'm...</i>

888
00:52:47,216 --> 00:52:50,576
<i>attracted to a woman strong enough
to hold my life in her hands.</i>

889
00:52:50,576 --> 00:52:53,600
<i>A woman who could hurt me at any time,</i>

890
00:52:53,600 --> 00:52:54,783
<i>but chooses not to.</i>

891
00:52:54,783 --> 00:52:57,469
[Kwon Se Ah, Current: Graduate student,
College of Physical Education]

892
00:52:57,469 --> 00:52:59,360
[Former: Women's Judo National Team Reserve]

893
00:52:59,360 --> 00:53:00,688
Kwon Se Ah, please.

894
00:53:00,688 --> 00:53:04,149
Take it easy. Don't kill them.

895
00:53:07,032 --> 00:53:08,783
Assistant Manager Ki!

896
00:53:08,783 --> 00:53:12,592
Yeah, I'm... I'm fine.

897
00:53:12,592 --> 00:53:14,016
Oh, no, what do I do?

898
00:53:14,016 --> 00:53:16,716
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

899
00:53:16,716 --> 00:53:18,288
Oh, dear.

900
00:53:18,288 --> 00:53:20,432
Oh, please don't come any closer.

901
00:53:20,432 --> 00:53:23,516
Please, just stay back.

902
00:53:26,229 --> 00:53:29,449
Oh, my tailbone... Oh...

903
00:53:29,449 --> 00:53:32,300
Jeez, I said stay back.

904
00:53:32,300 --> 00:53:34,783
Oh, my, are you okay?

905
00:53:34,783 --> 00:53:36,376
Oh...

906
00:53:36,376 --> 00:53:38,649
Stay still! Don't move!

907
00:53:38,649 --> 00:53:40,520
Darn, this is so embarrassing.

908
00:53:40,520 --> 00:53:42,512
Hey, take out that punk first!

909
00:53:42,512 --> 00:53:45,249
If you keep doing this,
I'm seriously going to call the police...

910
00:53:53,396 --> 00:53:55,816
No time for that.

911
00:53:57,820 --> 00:54:00,128
Oh, I'm terrified.

912
00:54:00,128 --> 00:54:03,449
Assistant Manager Ki,
that must've scared you, right?

913
00:54:06,849 --> 00:54:09,383
It... did.

914
00:54:10,488 --> 00:54:11,836
They just came out of nowhere.

915
00:54:11,836 --> 00:54:13,116
Hey, Kwon Se Ah!

916
00:54:13,116 --> 00:54:14,116
Huh? What?

917
00:54:14,116 --> 00:54:15,376
Hey, you!

918
00:54:15,376 --> 00:54:17,396
You...

919
00:54:17,396 --> 00:54:19,024
I knew you'd pull something like this.

920
00:54:19,024 --> 00:54:20,596
Huh?

921
00:54:20,596 --> 00:54:22,220
Hey!

922
00:54:22,220 --> 00:54:24,996
Hey, look at what you've done to him...

923
00:54:24,996 --> 00:54:27,779
I told you not to use
your techniques carelessly, right?

924
00:54:27,779 --> 00:54:30,840
Well... It just happened automatically.

925
00:54:30,840 --> 00:54:33,196
Hey, wake up!

926
00:54:33,196 --> 00:54:36,340
Are you okay? Hey!

927
00:54:36,340 --> 00:54:39,348
Wow, he passed out cold.

928
00:54:39,348 --> 00:54:41,636
Okay, no visible injuries.

929
00:54:41,636 --> 00:54:43,384
And you're not hurt anywhere, right?
Of course not.

930
00:54:43,384 --> 00:54:45,412
- Yeah.
- And you...

931
00:54:45,412 --> 00:54:48,216
barely had to lift a finger anyway.

932
00:54:58,276 --> 00:55:00,716
Oh, nice timing.

933
00:55:02,149 --> 00:55:04,149
[Beom Seong Hun, Current:
Nambu Station's Youngest Detective]

934
00:55:04,149 --> 00:55:06,149
[Former: Asian Games Gold Medalist
in Men's Judo, Special Police Hire]

935
00:55:06,149 --> 00:55:07,676
Don't move.

936
00:55:07,676 --> 00:55:12,512
You're under arrest for aggravated assault
and obstruction of official duties.

937
00:55:12,512 --> 00:55:16,332
You have the right
to remain silent and to an attorney.

938
00:55:16,332 --> 00:55:18,716
Oh, right. And anything stupid you say
can be used against you,

939
00:55:18,716 --> 00:55:20,716
so watch what you say.

940
00:55:22,349 --> 00:55:25,516
Mr. Tiger! True colors of a cop!
Champions of justice!

941
00:55:25,516 --> 00:55:26,776
- Hey!
- Hey!

942
00:55:26,776 --> 00:55:29,783
- Take them down and finish it!
- Take them down and finish it!

943
00:55:29,783 --> 00:55:31,249
- You remember?
- Hey, how do you know that?

944
00:55:31,249 --> 00:55:33,656
- This is nothing.
- Hey, what's going on here?

945
00:55:33,656 --> 00:55:35,604
- A throw.
- Hey, that's not right!

946
00:55:35,604 --> 00:55:37,408
No, you do it from here, like this!

947
00:55:37,408 --> 00:55:38,649
- Bam!
- Oh!

948
00:55:38,649 --> 00:55:41,792
What was that? Wow, you're good.

949
00:55:41,792 --> 00:55:44,304
- Of course, I'm a cop.
- Jeez.

950
00:55:44,304 --> 00:55:46,749
The police will be here soon...

951
00:55:48,964 --> 00:55:50,664
The kid...

952
00:55:51,364 --> 00:55:54,244
She's getting harder and harder to handle.

953
00:55:54,244 --> 00:55:57,964
Of course. The older they get,
the less they listen.

954
00:55:57,964 --> 00:56:01,612
I complained to my mom once,
and you know what she said?

955
00:56:01,612 --> 00:56:03,040
Did she say she'd scold your kid?

956
00:56:03,040 --> 00:56:05,949
She said my kid's
exactly like I was as a kid.

957
00:56:07,348 --> 00:56:10,783
She prayed for me
to have a daughter just like me,

958
00:56:12,048 --> 00:56:14,624
and her wish came true.

959
00:56:14,624 --> 00:56:16,716
That scared me more than anything.

960
00:56:16,716 --> 00:56:18,860
"A daughter who takes after me."

961
00:56:18,860 --> 00:56:22,364
Kids are half born that way
and half learn by watching.

962
00:56:22,364 --> 00:56:27,176
That's why they say,
"A child is a reflection of their parents."

963
00:56:27,176 --> 00:56:30,372
That saying, that one really hits me hard.

964
00:56:30,372 --> 00:56:33,132
I mean, isn't that a little unfair to me?

965
00:56:33,132 --> 00:56:38,316
All the time and effort I put into her...

966
00:56:39,996 --> 00:56:42,060
Jeez.

967
00:56:42,060 --> 00:56:43,388
Hold on.

968
00:56:43,388 --> 00:56:46,020
- It's your husband.
- Your husband.

969
00:56:46,020 --> 00:56:47,720
What?

970
00:56:48,516 --> 00:56:50,483
What time is it right now?

971
00:56:50,483 --> 00:56:52,924
Look at the clock.

972
00:56:52,924 --> 00:56:55,720
You come home at midnight every day,

973
00:56:55,720 --> 00:57:00,084
and you're complaining about
having to watch the kid one day early?

974
00:57:00,084 --> 00:57:01,516
What, her bath?

975
00:57:01,516 --> 00:57:05,204
Just give her a bath yourself.

976
00:57:05,204 --> 00:57:08,516
I don't know. Just put her to bed.

977
00:57:09,492 --> 00:57:11,416
Or whatever.

978
00:57:12,136 --> 00:57:15,572
Seriously, how is he exactly like my husband?

979
00:57:15,572 --> 00:57:17,016
We had this kid together,

980
00:57:17,016 --> 00:57:21,396
so why am I the one expected to do
all the parenting?

981
00:57:21,396 --> 00:57:22,776
If this is how it's going to be,

982
00:57:22,776 --> 00:57:24,568
he shouldn't have been begging
for a second kid.

983
00:57:24,568 --> 00:57:26,340
Well, my husband,

984
00:57:26,340 --> 00:57:29,712
even when I beg him to play
with the kids instead of drinking,

985
00:57:29,712 --> 00:57:32,156
all he ever says is, "Yeah, yeah."

986
00:57:32,156 --> 00:57:33,949
And one time,

987
00:57:34,880 --> 00:57:36,509
he called saying he was leaving,

988
00:57:36,509 --> 00:57:38,076
and then he took so long to show up
that I went down to check,

989
00:57:38,076 --> 00:57:41,083
and there he was, sleeping
in the parking lot. This guy, seriously.

990
00:57:41,083 --> 00:57:42,083
In the car?

991
00:57:42,083 --> 00:57:43,408
Yeah.

992
00:57:43,408 --> 00:57:44,928
What a gentleman.

993
00:57:44,928 --> 00:57:46,104
What?

994
00:57:46,104 --> 00:57:49,120
I got a call from the security office
once about Hye Ri's dad.

995
00:57:49,120 --> 00:57:51,283
They said he was snoring
away in the elevator.

996
00:57:51,283 --> 00:57:52,316
Oh, God.

997
00:57:52,316 --> 00:57:55,783
What if the kids learn from watching them?

998
00:57:56,788 --> 00:58:00,016
Then just raise them alone as I do.

999
00:58:07,272 --> 00:58:08,824
What about you, Yul's mom?

1000
00:58:08,824 --> 00:58:10,620
What?

1001
00:58:10,620 --> 00:58:12,232
Yul's dad.

1002
00:58:12,232 --> 00:58:14,340
I'm curious what kind of dad Yul has.

1003
00:58:14,340 --> 00:58:17,249
Yeah, me too. What's he like?

1004
00:58:18,728 --> 00:58:20,749
My husband?

1005
00:58:26,320 --> 00:58:27,968
Did my little girl get hurt a lot?

1006
00:58:27,968 --> 00:58:30,660
Yeah, it hurt a lot.

1007
00:58:30,660 --> 00:58:35,412
It's okay. I put some medicine on it,
so it'll get better soon.

1008
00:58:35,412 --> 00:58:39,049
What made you the saddest today, Yul?

1009
00:58:40,576 --> 00:58:42,416
Hye Ri cried today.

1010
00:58:42,416 --> 00:58:45,036
Oh, did seeing Hye Ri cry
make you the saddest?

1011
00:58:45,036 --> 00:58:48,228
- Yeah.
- Why did that make you so sad?

1012
00:58:48,228 --> 00:58:53,516
Because Mommy told me
to get along with my friends.

1013
00:58:53,516 --> 00:58:58,348
Oh, you wanted to get along
with your friend, but it didn't work out?

1014
00:58:58,348 --> 00:59:02,004
Yeah. But we shouldn't hurt our friends.

1015
00:59:02,004 --> 00:59:04,104
That's right. We shouldn't hurt our friends.

1016
00:59:04,104 --> 00:59:08,304
- No biting and no pushing, right?
- Yeah.

1017
00:59:08,304 --> 00:59:12,654
But sometimes things like that happen
when you're playing with friends.

1018
00:59:12,654 --> 00:59:13,880
What should you do then?

1019
00:59:13,880 --> 00:59:15,492
I should say "Sorry."

1020
00:59:15,492 --> 00:59:16,492
That's right.

1021
00:59:16,492 --> 00:59:20,772
Apologize, make up, and be friends again.

1022
00:59:20,772 --> 00:59:23,488
Yeah, I'll give them presents
and ask them to play with me.

1023
00:59:23,488 --> 00:59:26,232
Wow, your friends are going to love that.

1024
00:59:26,232 --> 00:59:29,880
Then how about we pick out presents
for your friends together tomorrow?

1025
00:59:29,880 --> 00:59:31,316
- Yeah.
- Good.

1026
00:59:31,316 --> 00:59:33,756
Now, what should we play?

1027
00:59:33,756 --> 00:59:34,816
Superman?

1028
00:59:34,816 --> 00:59:36,440
Alright, arms out! Superman!

1029
00:59:36,440 --> 00:59:38,283
Stretch!

1030
00:59:38,283 --> 00:59:40,216
Wow!

1031
00:59:43,884 --> 00:59:46,308
They say the one who throws the punch
sleeps like a baby.

1032
00:59:46,308 --> 00:59:49,983
Even the punk who threatened the chief
seems pretty darn comfortable.

1033
00:59:51,948 --> 00:59:54,083
Hey, Lee Dong Jin, wake up.

1034
00:59:55,496 --> 00:59:57,316
Wake up, now!

1035
00:59:59,996 --> 01:00:02,607
God, because of you,
I made a total fool of myself

1036
01:00:02,607 --> 01:00:04,564
in front of the commissioner today...

1037
01:00:04,564 --> 01:00:07,716
God, why did I ever bring in
a blockhead like you?

1038
01:00:07,716 --> 01:00:09,340
You...

1039
01:00:09,340 --> 01:00:11,552
You have to risk your life.

1040
01:00:11,552 --> 01:00:13,749
Otherwise, we're both going down.

1041
01:00:13,749 --> 01:00:14,764
What?

1042
01:00:14,764 --> 01:00:16,240
What are you doing?

1043
01:00:16,240 --> 01:00:18,649
Move it and pack your stuff, you punk!

1044
01:00:25,849 --> 01:00:28,668
<i>♪ Every day on the bus to school ♪</i>

1045
01:00:28,668 --> 01:00:32,116
<i>♪ I like the girl
who always sits in the same seat ♪</i>

1046
01:00:32,116 --> 01:00:35,536
<i>♪ I sometimes deliberately stand beside her ♪</i>

1047
01:00:35,536 --> 01:00:38,916
<i>♪ But somehow I feel like
I'm not good enough ♪</i>

1048
01:00:38,916 --> 01:00:42,249
<i>♪ No, I'm fine. Don't worry about it ♪</i>

1049
01:00:42,249 --> 01:00:45,683
- <i>♪ I don't have a boyfriend now ♪</i>
- Come on out.

1050
01:00:45,683 --> 01:00:50,000
<i>♪ But why won't you say a word? ♪</i>

1051
01:00:50,000 --> 01:00:53,249
<i>♪ I know you really need me ♪</i>

1052
01:00:53,249 --> 01:00:57,849
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1053
01:00:57,849 --> 01:01:02,592
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1054
01:01:02,592 --> 01:01:08,149
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1055
01:01:14,049 --> 01:01:16,983
<i>♪ Hesitating over something so simple ♪</i>

1056
01:01:16,983 --> 01:01:20,983
<i>♪ Watching you be so hopelessly
hesitant drives me crazy ♪</i>

1057
01:01:20,983 --> 01:01:25,049
<i>♪ You're too idealistic,
no woman is going to approach you ♪</i>

1058
01:01:25,049 --> 01:01:30,220
<i>♪ No woman is ever going
to make the first move ♪</i>

1059
01:01:30,220 --> 01:01:35,449
<i>♪ I'm no different, you know ♪</i>

1060
01:01:43,360 --> 01:01:46,416
I used to be better at this.

1061
01:01:48,749 --> 01:01:50,136
Yul's mom, sing one too.

1062
01:01:50,136 --> 01:01:51,749
- Oh, this is so much fun.
- Sing a song.

1063
01:01:51,749 --> 01:01:52,783
- Come on, sing.
- Me?

1064
01:01:52,783 --> 01:01:53,783
- No, I can't.
- We can't be the only ones singing.

1065
01:01:53,783 --> 01:01:54,783
- A song?
- Sing one!

1066
01:01:54,783 --> 01:01:59,049
- Sing a song!
- Sing a song!

1067
01:01:59,049 --> 01:02:03,883
[A Million Roses]

1068
01:02:08,048 --> 01:02:12,649
<i>♪ Long ago, from some distant star ♪</i>

1069
01:02:13,449 --> 01:02:19,316
<i>♪ When I came into this world ♪</i>

1070
01:02:19,316 --> 01:02:25,200
<i>♪ I heard a small voice ♪</i>

1071
01:02:25,200 --> 01:02:30,992
<i>♪ Telling me to come give love ♪</i>

1072
01:02:30,992 --> 01:02:34,392
<i>♪ That only blooms when you love ♪</i>

1073
01:02:34,392 --> 01:02:36,836
She's surprisingly romantic.

1074
01:02:36,836 --> 01:02:38,749
Exactly.

1075
01:02:38,749 --> 01:02:42,036
Why is she singing such a gloomy song?

1076
01:02:42,036 --> 01:02:44,649
She's killing the mood.

1077
01:02:44,649 --> 01:02:48,584
She's quite something.

1078
01:02:48,584 --> 01:02:54,372
<i>♪ Roses of love in bloom ♪</i>

1079
01:02:54,372 --> 01:03:00,088
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1080
01:03:00,088 --> 01:03:06,048
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1081
01:03:06,048 --> 01:03:11,916
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1082
01:03:11,916 --> 01:03:17,828
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1083
01:03:17,828 --> 01:03:23,680
<i>♪ Without a heart full of hate ♪</i>

1084
01:03:23,680 --> 01:03:28,849
<i>♪ When you give love without holding back ♪</i>

1085
01:03:29,460 --> 01:03:35,324
<i>♪ Millions and millions of roses bloom ♪</i>

1086
01:03:35,324 --> 01:03:40,383
<i>♪ And I can return to
our beautiful, beloved star ♪</i>

1087
01:03:44,136 --> 01:03:47,220
<i>A special task force has been formed</i>

1088
01:03:47,220 --> 01:03:50,400
<i>to apprehend the serial killer
known as Kingfisher.</i>

1089
01:03:50,400 --> 01:03:52,805
<i>Accordingly, the scattered
investigative information and personnel</i>

1090
01:03:52,805 --> 01:03:54,892
<i>from each case
are expected to be consolidated,</i>

1091
01:03:54,892 --> 01:04:00,083
<i>with dedicated staff assigned
to accelerate the Kingfisher investigation.</i>

1092
01:04:31,083 --> 01:04:33,316
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1093
01:04:33,316 --> 01:04:40,216
[Ok's Flower Shop]

1094
01:04:49,116 --> 01:04:52,549
<i>Will this finally end with
Kingfisher's arrest?</i>

1095
01:04:52,549 --> 01:04:57,316
<i>Attention is now focused on
the newly formed Kingfisher task force.</i>

1096
01:06:00,260 --> 01:06:02,349
The mugging during the World Cup?

1097
01:06:02,349 --> 01:06:05,849
I believe it could provide a clue
to Kingfisher's identity.

1098
01:06:05,849 --> 01:06:07,720
Do you remember the caller's voice?

1099
01:06:07,720 --> 01:06:09,496
The message on the first card
they sent was...

1100
01:06:09,496 --> 01:06:11,940
"I hope you find your own beautiful scenery."

1101
01:06:11,940 --> 01:06:14,183
Can you tell me anything
about the person sending the flowers?

1102
01:06:14,183 --> 01:06:16,083
Who is it? The person you saw that day.

1103
01:06:16,083 --> 01:06:17,083
Some woman.

1104
01:06:17,083 --> 01:06:18,728
Why are you looking for that woman?

1105
01:06:18,728 --> 01:06:21,536
She either witnessed Kingfisher,
or she is Kingfisher.

1106
01:06:21,536 --> 01:06:23,649
You should still have
the voice message on your phone.

1107
01:06:23,649 --> 01:06:24,649
Who's taking this case?

1108
01:06:24,649 --> 01:06:28,260
We'll set a trap around Gu Jung Yeol
before Kingfisher makes a move.

1109
01:06:28,260 --> 01:06:29,883
Client meeting starts.

1110
01:06:29,883 --> 01:06:32,483
Let's go catch Kingfisher.
